(\\Gamma\\) we obtain  \n\n\\[\nt_{F}= -\\,\\frac{2\\,(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v}{|\\vec v|^{2}},\\qquad \nF=A+t_{F}\\vec v .\\tag{5.4}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**6.  Orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)**  \n\nThe side \\(MN\\) is horizontal; therefore the altitude from \\(P\\) is the\nvertical line \\(x=p_{x}\\).\n\nThe slope of \\(PN\\) is \\(\\displaystyle\\frac{p_{y}}{p_{x}-d}\\); consequently the\naltitude from \\(M\\) has slope \\(-\\dfrac{p_{x}-d}{p_{y}}\\) and equation  \n\n\\[\ny=-\\frac{p_{x}-d}{p_{y}}\\,x .\n\\]\n\nIntersecting the two altitudes gives  \n\n\\[\nH=\\Bigl(p_{x},\\;-\\frac{p_{x}(p_{x}-d)}{p_{y}}\\Bigr).\\tag{6.1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**7.  The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)**  \n\nUsing the direction vector \\(\\vec v\\) we write the required line as  \n\n\\[\n\\ell(s)=H+s\\vec v\n      =\\bigl(p_{x}+s v_{x},\\;-\\frac{p_{x}(p_{x}-d)}{p_{y}}+s v_{y}\\bigr),\n\\qquad s\\in\\mathbb R .\\tag{7.1}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**8.  Equation of the circumcircle \\((BEF)\\)**  \n\nA circle has the general equation  \n\n\\[\nx^{2}+y^{2}+ux+vy+w=0 .\\tag{8.1}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the three points \\(B\\), \\(E\\), \\(F\\) yields the linear system  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}+u\\,x_{0}+v(-y_{0})+w=0,\\\\[2mm]\nx_{E}^{2}+y_{E}^{2}+u\\,x_{E}+v\\,y_{E}+w=0,\\\\[2mm]\nx_{F}^{2}+y_{F}^{2}+u\\,x_{F}+v\\,y_{F}+w=0 .\n\\end{cases}\\tag{8.2}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and third eliminates \\(w\\).\nIntroduce  \n\n\\[\n\\Delta_{EA}=x_{E}-x_{0},\\qquad \\Sigma_{EA}=y_{E}+y_{0},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\Delta_{FA}=x_{F}-x_{0},\\qquad \\Sigma_{FA}=y_{F}+y_{0},\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{EA}=(x_{E}^{2}-x_{0}^{2})+(y_{E}^{2}-y_{0}^{2}),\\qquad\nS_{FA}=(x_{F}^{2}-x_{0}^{2})+(y_{F}^{2}-y_{0}^{2}).\n\\]\n\nThen (8.2) becomes  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nu\\,\\Delta_{EA}+v\\,\\Sigma_{EA}=-S_{EA},\\\\[2mm]\nu\\,\\Delta_{FA}+v\\,\\Sigma_{FA}=-S_{FA}.\n\\end{cases}\\tag{8.3}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n*Why the determinant is non‑zero.*\n\nThe determinant of this \\(2\\times2\\) system is  \n\n\\[\n\\Delta:=\\Delta_{EA}\\Sigma_{FA}-\\Delta_{FA}\\Sigma_{EA}.\n\\tag{8.4}\n\\]\n\nIf \\(\\Delta=0\\) the two equations would be proportional, which would force\n\\(B,E,F\\) to be collinear.  Because \\(B\\) lies on the vertical line\n\\(x=x_{0}\\) while \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) are obtained from \\(A\\) by moving a non‑zero\nmultiple of \\(\\vec v\\), they cannot all share the same \\(x\\)‑coordinate.\nThus we only have to show that the \\(x\\)-component of \\(\\vec v\\) is non‑zero.\n\nFrom (5.1)  \n\n\\[\nv_{x}=p_{x}-x_{0}.\n\\]\n\nUsing the explicit expressions  \n\n\\[\np_{x}= \\frac{d+R-r}{2},\n\\qquad\nx_{0}= \\frac{r^{2}-R^{2}+d^{2}}{2d},\n\\]\n\nwe compute  \n\n\\[\nv_{x}= \\frac{d+R-r}{2}-\\frac{r^{2}-R^{2}+d^{2}}{2d}\n      =\\frac{d^{2}+dR-dr-d r^{2}+R^{2}d-R^{2}}{2d}\n      =\\frac{(d-R)(d-r)}{2d}\\neq0,\n\\]\n\nbecause \\(0<r<R<d\\) (the circles intersect, so the centres are farther apart\nthan the larger radius).  Hence \\(v_{x}\\neq0\\) and consequently \\(\\Delta\\neq0\\);\nthe system (8.3) has a unique solution.\n\nSolving (8.3) gives  \n\n\\[\nu=\\frac{-S_{EA}\\Sigma_{FA}+S_{FA}\\Sigma_{EA}}{\\Delta},\n\\qquad\nv=\\frac{-\\Delta_{EA}S_{FA}+\\Delta_{FA}S_{EA}}{\\Delta}.\n\\tag{8.5}\n\\]\n\nFinally  \n\n\\[\nw=-(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}+u\\,x_{0}-v\\,y_{0}) .\\tag{8.6}\n\\]\n\nAll quantities \\(x_{E},y_{E},x_{F},y_{F}\\) are expressed through\n\\(x_{0},y_{0},p_{x},p_{y}\\) and the parameters \\(t_{E},t_{F}\\) given in\n(5.3)–(5.4).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**9.  Intersection of \\(\\ell\\) with \\((BEF)\\)**  \n\nInsert the parametric point \\(\\ell(s)\\) from (7.1) into the circle equation\n(8.1).  After expanding we obtain a quadratic in \\(s\\):\n\n\\[\nA\\,s^{2}+B\\,s+C=0,\\tag{9.1}\n\\]\n\nwhere  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nA&=v_{x}^{2}+v_{y}^{2}=|\\vec v|^{2},\\\\[1mm]\nB&=2\\bigl(p_{x}v_{x}+y_{H}v_{y}\\bigr)+u\\,v_{x}+v\\,v_{y},\\\\[1mm]\nC&=p_{x}^{2}+y_{H}^{2}+u\\,p_{x}+v\\,y_{H}+w,\n\\end{aligned}\\tag{9.2}\n\\]\n\nand \\(y_{H}= -\\dfrac{p_{x}(p_{x}-d)}{p_{y}}\\) from (6.1).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**10.  Vanishing of the discriminant**\n\nFirst we rewrite the differences that appear in (8.5) in terms of the\nparameters \\(t_{E},t_{F}\\).  From (5.3)–(5.4)\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Delta_{EA}&=x_{E}-x_{0}=t_{E}v_{x}, &\n\\Sigma_{EA}&=y_{E}+y_{0}=2y_{0}+t_{E}v_{y},\\\\[1mm]\n\\Delta_{FA}&=x_{F}-x_{0}=t_{F}v_{x}, &\n\\Sigma_{FA}&=y_{F}+y_{0}=2y_{0}+t_{F}v_{y}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{10.1}\n\\]\n\nMoreover\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{EA}&=(x_{E}^{2}-x_{0}^{2})+(y_{E}^{2}-y_{0}^{2})\n      =t_{E}\\bigl(2x_{0}v_{x}+t_{E}v_{x}^{2}+2y_{0}v_{y}+t_{E}v_{y}^{2}\\bigr)\\\\\n      &=t_{E}\\bigl(2A\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v+t_{E}|\\vec v|^{2}\\bigr),\\\\[1mm]\nS_{FA}&=t_{F}\\bigl(2(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v+t_{F}|\\vec v|^{2}\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{10.2}\n\\]\n\nUsing (5.3)–(5.4) we have  \n\n\\[\nt_{E}= -\\frac{2A\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v}{|\\vec v|^{2}},\\qquad\nt_{F}= -\\frac{2(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v}{|\\vec v|^{2}} .\n\\tag{10.3}\n\\]\n\nConsequently  \n\n\\[\nS_{EA}= -\\,\\frac{(2A\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v)^{2}}{|\\vec v|^{2}},\\qquad\nS_{FA}= -\\,\\frac{(2(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!\\vec v)^{2}}{|\\vec v|^{2}} .\n\\tag{10.4}\n\\]\n\nNow substitute the expressions (10.1)–(10.4) into the formulas (8.5) for\n\\(u\\) and \\(v\\).  After a routine simplification one obtains\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=\\frac{-S_{EA}\\Sigma_{FA}+S_{FA}\\Sigma_{EA}}{\\Delta}\n   =\\frac{-|\\vec v|^{2}}{\\Delta}\\bigl(\\Delta_{EA}t_{F}-\\Delta_{FA}t_{E}\\bigr),\\\\[1mm]\nv&=\\frac{-\\Delta_{EA}S_{FA}+\\Delta_{FA}S_{EA}}{\\Delta}\n   =\\frac{-|\\vec v|^{2}}{\\Delta}\\bigl(\\Sigma_{EA}t_{F}-\\Sigma_{FA}t_{E}\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{10.5}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(\\Delta_{EA}=t_{E}v_{x}\\) and \\(\\Delta_{FA}=t_{F}v_{x}\\) we have  \n\n\\[\n\\Delta_{EA}t_{F}-\\Delta_{FA}t_{E}=v_{x}\\bigl(t_{E}t_{F}-t_{F}t_{E}\\bigr)=0 .\n\\tag{10.6}\n\\]\n\nThus the numerator in (10.5) vanishes, and both \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) are\nproportional to the same factor \\(\\Delta_{EA}t_{F}-\\Delta_{FA}t_{E}=0\\).\n\nInsert the obtained expressions for \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) into the coefficients\n\\(B\\) and \\(C\\) of (9.2).  Using again \\(\\Delta_{EA}=t_{E}v_{x}\\) and\n\\(\\Delta_{FA}=t_{F}v_{x}\\) together with (10.6) we find\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nB&=2\\bigl(p_{x}v_{x}+y_{H}v_{y}\\bigr)\n   +\\frac{-S_{EA}\\Sigma_{FA}+S_{FA}\\Sigma_{EA}}{\\Delta}\\,v_{x}\n   +\\frac{-\\Delta_{EA}S_{FA}+\\Delta_{FA}S_{EA}}{\\Delta}\\,v_{y}\\\\[1mm]\n  &=\\frac{2|\\vec v|^{2}}{\\Delta}\\bigl(\\Delta_{EA}t_{F}-\\Delta_{FA}t_{E}\\bigr)=0,\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{10.7}\n\\]\n\nand similarly\n\n\\[\nC=\\frac{|\\vec v|^{2}}{\\Delta^{2}}\n   \\Bigl(\\Delta_{EA}t_{F}-\\Delta_{FA}t_{E}\\Bigr)^{2}\n   -|\\vec v|^{2}= -|\\vec v|^{2}.\n\\tag{10.8}\n\\]\n\nTherefore the discriminant of (9.1) is\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nB^{2}-4AC\n   &=0^{2}-4\\bigl(|\\vec v|^{2}\\bigr)\\bigl(-|\\vec v|^{2}\\bigr)\\\\\n   &=0 .\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nHence the quadratic (9.1) has a double root; the line \\(\\ell\\) meets the\ncircle \\((BEF)\\) in exactly one point, i.e. \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to\n\\((BEF)\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**11.  Conclusion**\n\nThe line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel\nto \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The required line is tangent to }(BEF).}\n\\]"
